x86_64-linux  on Itanium a non-type template argument that is an expression of the parameters - V<N + M> - is spelled symbolically by clang, the expression between X and E (VIXplT_T0_EE, N+M as the sum of the two parameters), where cxx1 folds it to the concrete value V<3> (VILi3EE). The folded name is unique per instantiation and links with cxx1's own objects; spelling the expression needs a symbolic non-type argument through the mangler, its own step - the same XT_E family the member-template return still wants. Microsoft uses the substituted signature and is exact. What this case is about, the computed dimension folding correctly, is checked by run.sh on all three machines.
